{"id":"vol8-06","section":4,"path":"bank/listening/vol8-06/audio-4.m4a","model":"small","duration":401.61,"segments":[{"start":0.0,"end":3.06,"text":"Now turn to section 4 on page 7.","words":[["Now",0.0,0.34],["turn",0.34,0.6],["to",0.6,0.8],["section",0.8,1.04],["4",1.04,1.58],["on",1.58,2.2],["page",2.2,2.5],["7.",2.5,3.06]]},{"start":5.72,"end":14.66,"text":"Section 4 You will hear part of a student presentation about work on an archaeological site in southern Europe.","words":[["Section",5.72,5.98],["4",5.98,6.6],["You",6.6,8.12],["will",8.12,8.3],["hear",8.3,8.56],["part",8.56,8.88],["of",8.88,9.04],["a",9.04,9.18],["student",9.18,9.46],["presentation",9.46,10.16],["about",10.16,11.08],["work",11.08,11.52],["on",11.52,11.8],["an",11.8,11.96],["archaeological",11.96,12.5],["site",12.5,13.28],["in",13.28,13.68],["southern",13.68,14.08],["Europe.",14.08,14.66]]},{"start":15.38,"end":21.3,"text":"First you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40 on pages 7 and 8.","words":[["First",15.38,16.1],["you",16.1,16.3],["have",16.3,16.46],["some",16.46,16.6],["time",16.6,16.96],["to",16.96,17.18],["look",17.18,17.3],["at",17.3,17.42],["questions",17.42,17.76],["31",17.76,18.5],["to",18.5,18.72],["40",18.72,19.14],["on",19.14,19.84],["pages",19.84,20.12],["7",20.12,20.56],["and",20.56,20.96],["8.",20.96,21.3]]},{"start":71.84,"end":75.52,"text":"Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.","words":[["Now",71.84,72.2],["listen",72.2,72.52],["carefully",72.52,72.98],["and",72.98,73.32],["answer",73.32,73.7],["questions",73.7,74.1],["31",74.1,74.92],["to",74.92,75.16],["40.",75.16,75.52]]},{"start":75.52,"end":85.52,"text":"For my presentation, I'm going to talk to you about the archaeological dig I went on in the","words":[["For",75.52,76.58],["my",79.34,79.62],["presentation,",79.62,80.24],["I'm",81.06,81.36],["going",81.36,81.54],["to",81.54,81.72],["talk",81.72,81.96],["to",81.96,82.2],["you",82.2,82.36],["about",82.36,82.6],["the",82.6,82.8],["archaeological",82.8,83.4],["dig",83.4,83.98],["I",83.98,84.34],["went",84.34,84.54],["on",84.54,84.88],["in",84.88,85.42],["the",85.42,85.52]]},{"start":85.52,"end":92.82,"text":"summer at the site of Trimera in southern Europe near the Mediterranean Sea. The site is backed","words":[["summer",85.52,85.88],["at",85.88,86.46],["the",86.46,86.62],["site",86.62,86.9],["of",86.9,87.06],["Trimera",87.06,87.5],["in",87.5,88.32],["southern",88.32,88.6],["Europe",88.6,89.06],["near",89.06,89.54],["the",89.54,89.7],["Mediterranean",89.7,90.28],["Sea.",90.28,90.78],["The",91.76,91.98],["site",91.98,92.28],["is",92.28,92.54],["backed",92.54,92.82]]},{"start":92.82,"end":100.36,"text":"by a range of mountains to the north, overlooking a green fertile plain to the south. Let me","words":[["by",92.82,93.12],["a",93.12,93.3],["range",93.3,93.5],["of",93.5,93.72],["mountains",93.72,94.06],["to",94.06,94.38],["the",94.38,94.52],["north,",94.52,94.88],["overlooking",95.42,96.08],["a",96.08,96.46],["green",96.46,96.72],["fertile",96.72,97.24],["plain",97.24,97.8],["to",97.8,98.18],["the",98.18,98.32],["south.",98.32,98.68],["Let",99.76,100.18],["me",100.18,100.36]]},{"start":100.36,"end":106.46,"text":"first give you an idea of the history of the area and the growth of the city. The first","words":[["first",100.36,100.62],["give",100.62,100.9],["you",100.9,101.02],["an",101.02,101.16],["idea",101.16,101.44],["of",101.44,101.76],["the",101.76,101.88],["history",101.88,102.34],["of",102.34,102.68],["the",102.68,102.82],["area",102.82,103.14],["and",103.14,103.72],["the",103.72,103.88],["growth",103.88,104.14],["of",104.14,104.34],["the",104.34,104.46],["city.",104.46,104.7],["The",105.66,106.18],["first",106.18,106.46]]},{"start":106.46,"end":112.1,"text":"First evidence we have of human settlement in the Trimera area is of hunter-gatherers","words":[["First",106.46,106.54],["evidence",106.54,106.92],["we",106.92,107.22],["have",107.22,107.56],["of",107.56,107.8],["human",107.8,108.08],["settlement",108.08,108.58],["in",108.58,109.0],["the",109.0,109.16],["Trimera",109.16,109.5],["area",109.5,110.04],["is",110.04,110.78],["of",110.78,110.96],["hunter",110.96,111.26],["-gatherers",111.26,112.1]]},{"start":112.1,"end":114.6,"text":"around 12,000 years ago.","words":[["around",112.1,112.76],["12",112.76,113.24],[",000",113.24,113.94],["years",113.94,114.2],["ago.",114.2,114.6]]},{"start":115.54,"end":122.34,"text":"Later about 5,000 years ago, farmers settled along the many rivers which cut across the","words":[["Later",115.54,115.84],["about",115.84,116.34],["5",116.34,116.84],[",000",116.84,117.32],["years",117.32,117.6],["ago,",117.6,118.02],["farmers",118.44,118.92],["settled",118.92,119.3],["along",119.3,119.8],["the",119.8,120.02],["many",120.02,120.28],["rivers",120.28,120.66],["which",120.66,121.42],["cut",121.42,121.72],["across",121.72,122.02],["the",122.02,122.34]]},{"start":122.34,"end":130.7,"text":"plain and later still, from about 2,500 years ago, the city of Trimera was established","words":[["plain",122.34,122.66],["and",122.66,123.34],["later",123.34,123.6],["still,",123.6,124.06],["from",124.7,124.92],["about",124.92,125.3],["2",125.3,125.76],[",500",125.76,126.72],["years",126.72,127.42],["ago,",127.42,127.84],["the",128.4,128.54],["city",128.54,128.8],["of",128.8,129.12],["Trimera",129.12,129.62],["was",129.62,130.12],["established",130.12,130.7]]},{"start":131.12,"end":134.5,"text":"and it soon became a regional centre for trade.","words":[["and",131.12,131.54],["it",131.54,131.68],["soon",131.68,131.98],["became",131.98,132.42],["a",132.42,132.84],["regional",132.84,133.22],["centre",133.22,133.76],["for",133.76,134.08],["trade.",134.08,134.5]]},{"start":134.5,"end":144.02,"text":"The city was first invaded by the Greeks around 300 BC, then the Romans in 100 BC.","words":[["The",134.5,135.74],["city",135.74,136.04],["was",136.04,136.38],["first",136.38,136.72],["invaded",136.72,137.26],["by",137.26,137.84],["the",137.84,138.0],["Greeks",138.0,138.44],["around",138.44,139.1],["300",139.1,139.98],["BC,",139.98,140.48],["then",141.6,141.82],["the",141.82,142.02],["Romans",142.02,142.38],["in",142.38,142.88],["100",142.88,143.48],["BC.",143.48,144.02]]},{"start":145.32,"end":151.58,"text":"Under the Romans it became very prosperous and traded in grain, olives, and pottery.","words":[["Under",145.32,145.6],["the",145.6,145.76],["Romans",145.76,146.14],["it",146.14,146.6],["became",146.6,147.0],["very",147.0,147.44],["prosperous",147.44,148.02],["and",148.02,148.7],["traded",148.7,149.1],["in",149.1,149.4],["grain,",149.4,149.7],["olives,",150.38,150.68],["and",151.06,151.18],["pottery.",151.18,151.58]]},{"start":152.88,"end":160.62,"text":"Then in 518 AD an earthquake destroyed Trimera and the city was abandoned.","words":[["Then",152.88,153.38],["in",153.38,154.06],["518",154.06,154.9],["AD",154.9,155.68],["an",155.68,156.7],["earthquake",156.7,157.22],["destroyed",157.22,158.0],["Trimera",158.0,158.54],["and",158.54,159.3],["the",159.3,159.46],["city",159.46,159.72],["was",159.72,160.06],["abandoned.",160.06,160.62]]},{"start":161.6,"end":169.4,"text":"However, much of the city was covered with soil and rock by the earthquake, and so, luckily","words":[["However,",161.6,162.38],["much",162.9,163.36],["of",163.36,163.52],["the",163.52,163.64],["city",163.64,163.92],["was",163.92,164.26],["covered",164.26,164.68],["with",164.68,165.02],["soil",165.02,165.46],["and",165.46,165.9],["rock",165.9,166.26],["by",166.26,166.54],["the",166.54,166.66],["earthquake,",166.66,167.1],["and",167.66,168.08],["so,",168.08,168.5],["luckily",168.9,169.4]]},{"start":169.4,"end":174.0,"text":"for us archaeologists, many of the ruins survived intact.","words":[["for",169.4,169.78],["us",169.78,169.96],["archaeologists,",169.96,170.8],["many",171.44,171.8],["of",171.8,172.04],["the",172.04,172.2],["ruins",172.2,172.52],["survived",172.52,173.32],["intact.",173.32,174.0]]},{"start":176.1,"end":183.86,"text":"The first report on the ruins dates back to around 1706, when a French explorer passed","words":[["The",176.1,176.44],["first",176.44,176.68],["report",176.68,177.24],["on",177.24,177.6],["the",177.6,177.78],["ruins",177.78,178.22],["dates",178.22,178.52],["back",178.52,178.98],["to",178.98,179.26],["around",179.26,179.82],["1706,",179.82,181.2],["when",181.88,182.24],["a",182.24,182.4],["French",182.4,182.64],["explorer",182.64,183.32],["passed",183.32,183.86]]},{"start":183.86,"end":184.88,"text":"through the area.","words":[["through",183.86,184.26],["the",184.26,184.44],["area.",184.44,184.88]]},{"start":185.64,"end":189.54,"text":"He thought that what he was seeing were the ruins of a castle.","words":[["He",185.64,186.14],["thought",186.14,186.48],["that",186.48,186.7],["what",186.7,186.9],["he",186.9,187.14],["was",187.14,187.32],["seeing",187.32,187.76],["were",187.76,188.22],["the",188.22,188.38],["ruins",188.38,188.78],["of",188.78,189.04],["a",189.04,189.16],["castle.",189.16,189.54]]},{"start":189.54,"end":206.18,"text":"In the 19th century, a British archaeologist began to explore the site and later, a Polish count made the first map of the area and recorded some of the inscriptions which were visible on the surface.","words":[["In",189.54,190.96],["the",190.96,191.1],["19th",191.1,191.78],["century,",191.78,192.26],["a",192.76,192.94],["British",192.94,193.24],["archaeologist",193.24,194.18],["began",194.18,194.9],["to",194.9,195.22],["explore",195.22,195.66],["the",195.66,195.88],["site",195.88,196.22],["and",196.22,197.12],["later,",197.12,197.54],["a",198.1,198.34],["Polish",198.34,198.68],["count",198.68,199.4],["made",199.4,199.94],["the",199.94,200.12],["first",200.12,200.42],["map",200.42,200.82],["of",200.82,201.0],["the",201.0,201.12],["area",201.12,201.52],["and",201.52,202.34],["recorded",202.34,202.86],["some",202.86,203.18],["of",203.18,203.34],["the",203.34,203.44],["inscriptions",203.44,204.0],["which",204.0,204.74],["were",204.74,204.9],["visible",204.9,205.28],["on",205.28,205.72],["the",205.72,205.82],["surface.",205.82,206.18]]},{"start":207.3,"end":216.06,"text":"However, it was not until 1982 that a Swedish archaeologist made a full survey of the ruins of Tremora.","words":[["However,",207.3,207.92],["it",208.36,208.62],["was",208.62,208.76],["not",208.76,209.02],["until",209.02,209.42],["1982",209.42,210.3],["that",210.3,211.3],["a",211.3,211.48],["Swedish",211.48,211.9],["archaeologist",211.9,212.9],["made",212.9,213.46],["a",213.46,213.64],["full",213.64,213.92],["survey",213.92,214.44],["of",214.44,214.8],["the",214.8,214.98],["ruins",214.98,215.32],["of",215.32,215.66],["Tremora.",215.66,216.06]]},{"start":217.38,"end":222.7,"text":"The first remains to be excavated were identified as those of the market.","words":[["The",217.38,218.14],["first",218.14,218.46],["remains",218.46,218.98],["to",218.98,219.44],["be",219.44,219.58],["excavated",219.58,220.22],["were",220.22,220.54],["identified",220.54,220.98],["as",220.98,221.56],["those",221.56,221.84],["of",221.84,222.12],["the",222.12,222.24],["market.",222.24,222.7]]},{"start":223.7,"end":229.7,"text":"Archaeologists were trying to establish how trade was organized here and the type of goods which","words":[["Archaeologists",223.7,224.46],["were",224.46,224.72],["trying",224.72,225.1],["to",225.1,225.28],["establish",225.28,225.72],["how",225.72,226.18],["trade",226.18,226.64],["was",226.64,226.82],["organized",226.82,227.34],["here",227.34,227.84],["and",227.84,228.46],["the",228.46,228.6],["type",228.6,228.88],["of",228.88,229.04],["goods",229.04,229.4],["which",229.4,229.7]]},{"start":229.7,"end":237.08,"text":"were commonly bought and sold. In and around this area various examples of silver coins have","words":[["were",229.7,229.86],["commonly",229.86,230.3],["bought",230.3,230.7],["and",230.7,231.02],["sold.",231.02,231.4],["In",232.66,232.9],["and",232.9,233.04],["around",233.04,233.36],["this",233.36,233.64],["area",233.64,234.06],["various",234.06,234.82],["examples",234.82,235.42],["of",235.42,235.74],["silver",235.74,236.14],["coins",236.14,236.82],["have",236.82,237.08]]},{"start":237.08,"end":245.6,"text":"come to light. During the Roman period it appears that the city was completely reorganized. The","words":[["come",237.08,237.34],["to",237.34,237.5],["light.",237.5,237.78],["During",238.68,239.44],["the",239.44,239.68],["Roman",239.68,240.02],["period",240.02,240.58],["it",240.58,241.28],["appears",241.28,241.7],["that",241.7,241.92],["the",241.92,242.04],["city",242.04,242.3],["was",242.3,242.62],["completely",242.62,243.34],["reorganized.",243.34,244.58],["The",245.06,245.6]]},{"start":245.6,"end":248.9,"text":"The public squares were paved, as were the main streets.","words":[["The",245.6,245.66],["public",245.66,245.88],["squares",245.88,246.26],["were",246.26,246.66],["paved,",246.66,247.1],["as",247.58,247.88],["were",247.88,248.08],["the",248.08,248.22],["main",248.22,248.46],["streets.",248.46,248.9]]},{"start":250.18,"end":256.26,"text":"There is also some proof to suggest that textile production was an important industry.","words":[["There",250.18,250.58],["is",250.58,250.72],["also",250.72,251.24],["some",251.24,251.56],["proof",251.56,251.96],["to",251.96,252.28],["suggest",252.28,252.72],["that",252.72,253.02],["textile",253.02,253.68],["production",253.68,254.38],["was",254.38,255.04],["an",255.04,255.18],["important",255.18,255.6],["industry.",255.6,256.26]]},{"start":257.32,"end":262.84,"text":"The huge prosperity during this period was helped by the fact that the city was responsible","words":[["The",257.32,257.62],["huge",257.62,258.02],["prosperity",258.02,258.62],["during",258.62,259.18],["this",259.18,259.42],["period",259.42,259.84],["was",259.84,260.48],["helped",260.48,260.82],["by",260.82,261.06],["the",261.06,261.22],["fact",261.22,261.44],["that",261.44,261.62],["the",261.62,261.74],["city",261.74,261.98],["was",261.98,262.2],["responsible",262.2,262.84]]},{"start":262.84,"end":266.34,"text":"for provisioning the Roman army in the eastern region.","words":[["for",262.84,263.4],["provisioning",263.4,264.14],["the",264.14,264.26],["Roman",264.26,264.52],["army",264.52,265.02],["in",265.02,265.4],["the",265.4,265.52],["eastern",265.52,265.88],["region.",265.88,266.34]]},{"start":271.72,"end":276.7,"text":"Now what I'd like to do is talk about some of the more important buildings in some","words":[["Now",271.72,272.08],["what",272.08,272.32],["I'd",272.32,272.54],["like",272.54,272.68],["to",272.68,272.92],["do",272.92,273.18],["is",273.18,273.74],["talk",273.74,273.98],["about",273.98,274.28],["some",274.28,274.5],["of",274.5,274.66],["the",274.66,274.74],["more",274.74,274.9],["important",274.9,275.44],["buildings",275.44,275.88],["in",275.88,276.36],["some",276.36,276.7]]},{"start":276.7,"end":277.22,"text":"detail.","words":[["detail.",276.7,277.22]]},{"start":278.36,"end":286.42,"text":"First of all, the Doric house. This Greek building is located to the east of the city, near the","words":[["First",278.36,278.96],["of",278.96,279.22],["all,",279.22,279.5],["the",279.94,279.98],["Doric",279.98,280.48],["house.",280.48,280.8],["This",282.0,282.46],["Greek",282.46,282.78],["building",282.78,283.26],["is",283.26,283.58],["located",283.58,284.04],["to",284.04,284.52],["the",284.52,284.68],["east",284.68,284.94],["of",284.94,285.1],["the",285.1,285.2],["city,",285.2,285.48],["near",286.06,286.28],["the",286.28,286.42]]},{"start":286.42,"end":292.82,"text":"copper mines. This building is where the local population would come to get their water. The","words":[["copper",286.42,286.7],["mines.",286.7,287.12],["This",288.02,288.36],["building",288.36,288.72],["is",288.72,289.0],["where",289.0,289.22],["the",289.22,289.38],["local",289.38,289.66],["population",289.66,290.38],["would",290.38,290.6],["come",290.6,290.9],["to",290.9,291.1],["get",291.1,291.26],["their",291.26,291.44],["water.",291.44,291.78],["The",292.52,292.82]]},{"start":292.82,"end":298.38,"text":"fact that the ruins were so well preserved has meant that the team of archaeologists excavating","words":[["fact",292.82,293.04],["that",293.04,293.26],["the",293.26,293.36],["ruins",293.36,293.66],["were",293.66,293.92],["so",293.92,294.14],["well",294.14,294.38],["preserved",294.38,294.86],["has",294.86,295.58],["meant",295.58,295.84],["that",295.84,296.06],["the",296.06,296.18],["team",296.18,296.5],["of",296.5,296.66],["archaeologists",296.66,297.46],["excavating",297.46,298.38]]},{"start":298.38,"end":305.32,"text":"the site has been able to partially reconstruct the building. The remains of a theater are to","words":[["the",298.38,298.6],["site",298.6,298.92],["has",298.92,299.38],["been",299.38,299.56],["able",299.56,299.92],["to",299.92,300.1],["partially",300.1,300.64],["reconstruct",300.64,301.32],["the",301.32,301.8],["building.",301.8,302.12],["The",303.22,303.56],["remains",303.56,303.86],["of",303.86,304.1],["a",304.1,304.18],["theater",304.18,304.62],["are",304.62,305.18],["to",305.18,305.32]]},{"start":305.32,"end":311.3,"text":"be found in the northwest of the city adjacent to the river, where a magnificent bridge made","words":[["be",305.32,305.44],["found",305.44,305.78],["in",305.78,306.14],["the",306.14,306.24],["northwest",306.24,306.64],["of",306.64,307.08],["the",307.08,307.18],["city",307.18,307.46],["adjacent",307.46,308.26],["to",308.26,308.64],["the",308.64,308.76],["river,",308.76,309.04],["where",309.5,309.8],["a",309.8,309.94],["magnificent",309.94,310.4],["bridge",310.4,311.0],["made",311.0,311.3]]},{"start":311.3,"end":318.68,"text":"of stone has recently been unearthed. In Roman times, the theatre appears to have been extended","words":[["of",311.3,311.42],["stone",311.42,311.86],["has",311.86,312.3],["recently",312.3,312.82],["been",312.82,313.24],["unearthed.",313.24,314.0],["In",315.0,315.32],["Roman",315.32,315.62],["times,",315.62,316.12],["the",316.6,316.74],["theatre",316.74,317.0],["appears",317.0,317.52],["to",317.52,317.74],["have",317.74,317.9],["been",317.9,318.06],["extended",318.06,318.68]]},{"start":319.17,"end":323.02,"text":"and may have been able to take up to 5,000 spectators.","words":[["and",319.17,319.52],["may",319.52,319.78],["have",319.78,320.0],["been",320.0,320.18],["able",320.18,320.46],["to",320.46,320.64],["take",320.64,320.88],["up",320.88,321.1],["to",321.1,321.26],["5",321.26,321.68],[",000",321.68,322.26],["spectators.",322.26,323.02]]},{"start":324.73,"end":331.4,"text":"In the southwestern corner of the city are the remains of an elegant stairway. It dates","words":[["In",324.73,325.08],["the",325.08,325.2],["southwestern",325.2,326.02],["corner",326.02,326.34],["of",326.34,326.52],["the",326.52,326.62],["city",326.62,326.92],["are",326.92,327.52],["the",327.52,327.66],["remains",327.66,328.04],["of",328.04,328.52],["an",328.52,328.66],["elegant",328.66,329.02],["stairway.",329.02,329.88],["It",330.54,331.04],["dates",331.04,331.4]]},{"start":331.4,"end":339.56,"text":"back to about 37 AD. The stairway is decorated with sculptures of lions as opposed to bears","words":[["back",331.4,331.7],["to",331.7,331.92],["about",331.92,332.24],["37",332.24,332.82],["AD.",332.82,333.58],["The",334.88,335.16],["stairway",335.16,335.66],["is",335.66,335.88],["decorated",335.88,336.28],["with",336.28,336.76],["sculptures",336.76,337.2],["of",337.2,337.66],["lions",337.66,338.06],["as",338.06,338.54],["opposed",338.54,338.86],["to",338.86,339.18],["bears",339.18,339.56]]},{"start":339.56,"end":345.62,"text":"found in other parts of the site. This is possibly because of trading links with Africa.","words":[["found",339.56,340.18],["in",340.18,340.34],["other",340.34,340.6],["parts",340.6,341.02],["of",341.02,341.16],["the",341.16,341.26],["site.",341.26,341.56],["This",342.48,342.84],["is",342.84,343.02],["possibly",343.02,343.64],["because",343.64,344.06],["of",344.06,344.24],["trading",344.24,344.56],["links",344.56,344.96],["with",344.96,345.3],["Africa.",345.3,345.62]]},{"start":346.98,"end":353.12,"text":"Finally, the most recent discovery has been at the site of the Roman baths in the","words":[["Finally,",346.98,347.66],["the",348.34,348.42],["most",348.42,348.66],["recent",348.66,349.1],["discovery",349.1,349.7],["has",349.7,350.2],["been",350.2,350.44],["at",350.44,350.56],["the",350.56,350.68],["site",350.68,351.0],["of",351.0,351.24],["the",351.24,351.36],["Roman",351.36,351.62],["baths",351.62,352.42],["in",352.42,353.0],["the",353.0,353.12]]},{"start":353.12,"end":359.42,"text":"central area of Tremora. Here, a huge statue of an emperor from the Roman period was","words":[["central",353.12,353.46],["area",353.46,353.88],["of",353.88,354.08],["Tremora.",354.08,354.48],["Here,",355.34,355.74],["a",356.0,356.12],["huge",356.12,356.4],["statue",356.4,356.82],["of",356.82,357.12],["an",357.12,357.26],["emperor",357.26,357.6],["from",357.6,357.96],["the",357.96,358.12],["Roman",358.12,358.36],["period",358.36,358.84],["was",358.84,359.42]]},{"start":359.42,"end":365.6,"text":"excavated. It appears to have been carved in pieces and then taken to the site","words":[["excavated.",359.42,360.02],["It",360.72,361.48],["appears",361.48,361.92],["to",361.92,362.24],["have",362.24,362.38],["been",362.38,362.54],["carved",362.54,362.96],["in",362.96,363.22],["pieces",363.22,363.68],["and",363.68,364.4],["then",364.4,364.6],["taken",364.6,364.96],["to",364.96,365.18],["the",365.18,365.32],["site",365.32,365.6]]},{"start":365.6,"end":372.38,"text":"and put together. The statue is very finely detailed and the recent discovery","words":[["and",365.6,365.98],["put",365.98,366.18],["together.",366.18,366.6],["The",367.64,368.1],["statue",368.1,368.6],["is",368.6,369.08],["very",369.08,369.4],["finely",369.4,369.92],["detailed",369.92,370.56],["and",370.56,371.48],["the",371.48,371.62],["recent",371.62,371.88],["discovery",371.88,372.38]]},{"start":372.38,"end":378.44,"text":"of marble toes and the hem of a dress suggests that a companion statue may","words":[["of",372.38,372.7],["marble",372.7,373.08],["toes",373.08,373.66],["and",373.66,374.32],["the",374.32,374.48],["hem",374.48,374.7],["of",374.7,374.84],["a",374.84,375.0],["dress",375.0,375.38],["suggests",375.38,376.16],["that",376.16,376.58],["a",376.58,376.68],["companion",376.68,377.22],["statue",377.22,377.78],["may",377.78,378.44]]},{"start":378.44,"end":385.32,"text":"also be buried in the bath site. During the dig I was responsible for many","words":[["also",378.44,378.82],["be",378.82,379.02],["buried",379.02,379.36],["in",379.36,379.72],["the",379.72,379.82],["bath",379.82,380.08],["site.",380.08,380.6],["During",381.64,382.36],["the",382.36,382.56],["dig",382.56,382.86],["I",382.86,383.66],["was",383.66,383.84],["responsible",383.84,384.48],["for",384.48,384.98],["many",384.98,385.32]]},{"start":388.2,"end":390.74,"text":"That is the end of section 4.","words":[["That",388.2,389.1],["is",389.1,389.28],["the",389.28,389.42],["end",389.42,389.78],["of",389.78,389.96],["section",389.96,390.2],["4.",390.2,390.74]]},{"start":391.52,"end":394.4,"text":"You now have half a minute to check your answers.","words":[["You",391.52,391.7],["now",391.7,392.0],["have",392.0,392.36],["half",392.36,392.7],["a",392.7,392.9],["minute",392.9,393.16],["to",393.16,393.5],["check",393.5,393.82],["your",393.82,394.04],["answers.",394.04,394.4]]}]}